IMPORT prelude

-- Defamation Act 2005 (Western Australia) -- what the Act means for a person who has been defamed, from the seat of that
-- person.
--
-- SEAT: the person defamed ("May I sue, or may my company? Is my letter a concerns notice, and what does it do? Can the
-- publisher still offer to make amends, and if I accept, can I still sue? Which defences can the publisher raise? What is the
-- most I can get for non-economic loss? By when must I sue?"). Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask
-- it. What the Act tells a court or a publisher is encoded as what it means for that person.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4 ("substantially true"); s 7 (no proof of special damage); s 9 (corporations: no cause of action
-- unless an "excluded corporation"; the individual's own claim kept by s 9(5)); s 10 (no cause of action about, or against,
-- a deceased person); s 12 (the publisher and the aggrieved person); s 14 (when an offer to make amends may be made; the
-- concerns notice; the further particulars notice and the 14 days); s 15(1)(a)-(f) (what an offer must contain); s 16(4),
-- (5) (a renewed offer); s 17(1) (effect of acceptance); s 18(1) (the defence for a reasonable offer not accepted); s 23
-- (leave for further proceedings); s 25 (justification); s 26 (contextual truth); s 31(1), (4)(a), (5) (honest opinion of
-- the publisher); s 33 (triviality); s 35(1), (2), (4), (7) (the cap on damages for non-economic loss, aggravated damages,
-- indexing rounded to $500); s 37 (no exemplary or punitive damages). From the Limitation Act 2005 (WA), brought in because
-- the Defamation Act sets no time limit: s 15 (one year from publication), s 40 (the court's extension, up to 3 years).
--
-- Edition: the Defamation Act 2005 (No. 44 of 2005) as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_602.txt
-- (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 602, retrieved 2026-09-07). Its compilation table lists only the Act itself (assent 19 Dec
-- 2005, commencement 1 Jan 2006): NO AMENDMENT. The deposit therefore has no s 10A (serious harm), no ss 12A-12B (concerns
-- notice as a precondition to suing), no s 4 definition of "digital intermediary", and no public interest defence (s 29A);
-- the concerns notice it knows is the one in s 14(2), which only starts the publisher's 28 days to offer amends. The
-- Limitation Act 2005 (No. 19 of 2005) is used as deposited at
-- ../../../limitation-act-2005/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47979.txt (mrdoc 47979, retrieved 2026-09-07). No regulations
-- are used (none is made under s 45 for the cap).
--
-- NUMBERS THAT ARE INPUTS. The maximum damages amount at the time damages are awarded is the Minister's yearly Gazette
-- order (s 35(3)); no order is deposited, so the amount is an input. The text's starting figure ($250 000) is encoded, and
-- so is the rule for the next declared amount (s 35(4), (7)), with the Statistician's percentage change as an input.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 11 (choice of law); ss 13(2)-(4) (limited offers; joint publishers; without prejudice); s 15(1)(g), (2)-(4)
-- (optional content; compensation; the court's powers after acceptance); s 16(1)-(3) (withdrawal); s 17(2), (3) (expenses
-- after acceptance); s 18(2) (what the court weighs in reasonableness: asked as the court's finding); s 19 (inadmissibility);
-- s 20 (apologies); ss 21, 22 (juries); ss 27-30 (absolute privilege, public documents, fair report, qualified privilege);
-- s 31(2), (3) (opinions of employees, agents and commentators); s 32 (innocent dissemination); s 34, s 36, ss 38, 39
-- (assessment and mitigation); s 40 (costs); Part 5 (proof, notices, regulations, repeal, savings); Schedule 4 (criminal
-- defamation, The Criminal Code s 345); the Limitation Act's s 8 (pre-2006 publications). Whether matter is defamatory at
-- all is the general law's question (s 6): it is asked as a fact, never decided.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the person defamed, with the design defaults
-- ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. Money is in dollars. Periods are in the unit the name says (days, months).

§ `Defamation Act 2005 -- the person defamed`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `ss 9, 10, 23 -- may I sue at all`

-- s 9(1): "A corporation has no cause of action for defamation in relation to the publication of defamatory matter about the
-- corporation unless it was an excluded corporation at the time of the publication."
-- s 9(2): "A corporation is an excluded corporation if -- (a) the objects for which it is formed do not include obtaining
-- financial gain for its members or corporators; or (b) it employs fewer than 10 persons and is not related to another
-- corporation, and the corporation is not a public body."
-- s 9(3): part-time employees count "as an appropriate fraction of a fulltime equivalent", so the headcount is asked as
-- full-time equivalents. s 9(4): "related" is as in s 50 of the Corporations Act 2001 (a borrowed term, asked as a fact).
-- s 9(6): "public body means a local government body or other governmental or public authority constituted by or under a
-- law of any country."
DECLARE `The corporation at the time of publication` HAS
    `its objects include obtaining financial gain for its members`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(2)(a)
    `the number of full-time-equivalent employees`                           IS A NUMBER    -- s 9(2)(b), (3)
    `it is related to another corporation (Corporations Act s 50)`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(2)(b), (4)
    `it is a public body`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(2), (6)

-- An "excluded corporation" is the kind of company the Act still lets sue: a not-for-profit, or a small unrelated company,
-- and in either case not a government body.
@export Is my company an "excluded corporation", one that may sue for defamation (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `the company` IS A `The corporation at the time of publication` @desc Your company's objects, its full-time-equivalent headcount when the matter was published, whether it is related to another company, and whether it is a public body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my company an excluded corporation` IF
        (    (NOT (`the company`'s `its objects include obtaining financial gain for its members`))
          OR (     `the company`'s `the number of full-time-equivalent employees` LESS THAN 10
               AND (NOT (`the company`'s `it is related to another corporation (Corporations Act s 50)`))))
    AND (NOT (`the company`'s `it is a public body`))

-- Who would bring the claim. s 9(5): s 9(1) "does not affect any cause of action for defamation that an individual
-- associated with a corporation has in relation to the publication of defamatory matter about the individual even if the
-- publication of the same matter also defames the corporation." s 10: "A person (including a personal representative of a
-- deceased person) cannot assert, continue or enforce a cause of action for defamation in relation to -- (a) the publication
-- of defamatory matter about a deceased person ...; or (b) the publication of defamatory matter by a person who has died
-- since publishing the matter."
DECLARE `Whose reputation` IS ONE OF
    `mine, and I am alive`
    `my company's`
    `a person who has died (I would sue as family or personal representative)`

-- "Defamatory" is the general law's word (s 6(2)); whether the matter carries a defamatory imputation is asked as a fact.
-- s 7(2): "the publication of defamatory matter of any kind is actionable without proof of special damage", so no loss
-- needs to be shown. (The deposited edition has no serious harm element; see the header.)
DECLARE `The publication` HAS
    `whose reputation the matter is about`                                   IS A `Whose reputation`
    `the matter carries a defamatory imputation about them`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- general law, s 6
    `the company`                                                            IS A `The corporation at the time of publication`
    `the publisher has died since publishing it`                             IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 10(b)
    `I have already sued this publisher for damages over this or like matter`  IS A BOOLEAN -- s 23
    `the court has given leave for the further proceedings`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 23

DECLARE `Whether I may sue` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a cause of action for defamation, without proof of special damage (ss 7, 8)`
    `yes, but only with the leave of the court, having sued this publisher over this matter before (s 23)`
    `no: a corporation that was not an excluded corporation at the time of publication (s 9(1))`
    `no: no cause of action about a deceased person (s 10(a))`
    `no: no cause of action against a publisher who has died since publishing (s 10(b))`
    `no: the matter carries no defamatory imputation (general law)`

@export May I (or my company) sue for defamation over this publication (ss 7-10, 23)?
GIVEN `the publication` IS A `The publication` @desc Whose reputation the matter is about, whether it carries a defamatory imputation, the company's facts if it is about your company, whether the publisher has died, and whether you have sued over it before
GIVETH A `Whether I may sue`
DECIDE `May I sue for defamation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the publication`'s `the matter carries a defamatory imputation about them`))
            THEN `no: the matter carries no defamatory imputation (general law)`
        IF `the publication`'s `whose reputation the matter is about` EQUALS `a person who has died (I would sue as family or personal representative)`
            THEN `no: no cause of action about a deceased person (s 10(a))`
        IF `the publication`'s `the publisher has died since publishing it`
            THEN `no: no cause of action against a publisher who has died since publishing (s 10(b))`
        IF     `the publication`'s `whose reputation the matter is about` EQUALS `my company's`
           AND (NOT (`Is my company an excluded corporation` (`the publication`'s `the company`)))
            THEN `no: a corporation that was not an excluded corporation at the time of publication (s 9(1))`
        IF     `the publication`'s `I have already sued this publisher for damages over this or like matter`
           AND (NOT (`the publication`'s `the court has given leave for the further proceedings`))
            THEN `yes, but only with the leave of the court, having sued this publisher over this matter before (s 23)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: a cause of action for defamation, without proof of special damage (ss 7, 8)`

§§ `Limitation Act 2005 ss 15, 40 -- by when must I sue`

-- Limitation Act 2005 s 15: "An action relating to the publication of defamatory matter cannot be commenced if one year has
-- elapsed since the publication."
-- s 40(2): the court, "if satisfied that it was not reasonable in the circumstances for the plaintiff to have commenced an
-- action in relation to the matter complained of within one year from the publication, must extend the time".
-- s 40(3): it "cannot be commenced if 3 years have elapsed since the publication."
-- ss 34, 37, 38(4), 41(4): the suspensions for minors and for mental disability, and the fraud extension, do not apply to
-- defamation. Time is counted in whole months: 12 full months is the year (the encoder's unit; a day count would decide the
-- anniversary itself).
DECLARE `My time to sue` IS ONE OF
    `in time: less than one year since publication (Limitation Act s 15)`
    `out of time unless the court extends it, which it must if satisfied it was not reasonable to sue within the year (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
    `in time only because the court has extended it (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
    `too late: 3 years have elapsed since publication (Limitation Act s 40(3))`

@export Am I still in time to sue for defamation (Limitation Act 2005 ss 15, 40)?
GIVEN `full months since publication` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months have passed since the matter was published
      `the court has extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has already extended your time under Limitation Act s 40
GIVETH A `My time to sue`
DECIDE `Am I in time to sue` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `full months since publication` AT LEAST 36
            THEN `too late: 3 years have elapsed since publication (Limitation Act s 40(3))`
        IF `full months since publication` LESS THAN 12
            THEN `in time: less than one year since publication (Limitation Act s 15)`
        IF `the court has extended my time`
            THEN `in time only because the court has extended it (Limitation Act s 40(2))`
        OTHERWISE `out of time unless the court extends it, which it must if satisfied it was not reasonable to sue within the year (Limitation Act s 40(2))`

§§ `s 14 -- the concerns notice`

-- s 14(2): "A notice is a concerns notice for the purposes of this section if the notice -- (a) is in writing; and (b)
-- informs the publisher of the defamatory imputations that the aggrieved person considers are or may be carried about the
-- aggrieved person by the matter in question (the imputations of concern)."
-- s 14(3)-(5): if I fail "to particularise the imputations of concern adequately", the publisher may give me "a further
-- particulars notice"; I "must provide the reasonable further particulars ... within 14 days (or any further period agreed by
-- the publisher and aggrieved person)"; if I do not, I am "taken not to have given the publisher a concerns notice".
-- Whether I particularised adequately is the publisher's call in the first place; the encoding asks only whether a further
-- particulars notice was given and when I answered it.
DECLARE `My notice to the publisher` HAS
    `it is in writing`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 14(2)(a)
    `it tells the publisher the defamatory imputations I say it carries about me`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 14(2)(b)
    `the publisher gave me a further particulars notice`                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 14(3)
    `days I took to give the further particulars`                            IS A NUMBER    -- s 14(4); a large number if never
    `extra days the publisher agreed to`                                     IS A NUMBER    -- s 14(4); 0 if none

GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My notice to the publisher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I answered the further particulars notice in time` IF
    `the notice`'s `days I took to give the further particulars` AT MOST (14 PLUS `the notice`'s `extra days the publisher agreed to`)

@export Is my letter to the publisher a "concerns notice" (s 14(2)-(5))?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My notice to the publisher` @desc Whether your notice is in writing and names the imputations, and whether the publisher asked for further particulars and how quickly you gave them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice a concerns notice` IF
        `the notice`'s `it is in writing`
    AND `the notice`'s `it tells the publisher the defamatory imputations I say it carries about me`
    AND (    (NOT (`the notice`'s `the publisher gave me a further particulars notice`))
          OR `I answered the further particulars notice in time` `the notice`)

DECLARE `What my notice does` IS ONE OF
    `it starts the publisher's 28 days to make an offer to make amends (s 14(1)(a)); this edition does not require it before I sue`
    `nothing under the Act: it is not a concerns notice (s 14(2), (5)); this edition does not require one before I sue`

-- "What must I do before suing?" In the deposited edition: nothing under this Act. The concerns notice appears only in
-- s 14, where 28 days from it close the publisher's time for an offer to make amends. (The 2021 model amendments, which make
-- a concerns notice and a waiting period a precondition to suing, are not in the deposit.)
@export What does my concerns notice do, and must I give one before suing (s 14)?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My notice to the publisher` @desc Whether your notice is in writing and names the imputations, and whether the publisher asked for further particulars and how quickly you gave them
GIVETH A `What my notice does`
DECIDE `What does my notice do` IS
    IF `Is my notice a concerns notice` `the notice`
        THEN `it starts the publisher's 28 days to make an offer to make amends (s 14(1)(a)); this edition does not require it before I sue`
        ELSE `nothing under the Act: it is not a concerns notice (s 14(2), (5)); this edition does not require one before I sue`

§§ `ss 14, 16 -- when the publisher may offer to make amends`

-- s 14(1): "An offer to make amends cannot be made if -- (a) 28 days have elapsed since the publisher was given a concerns
-- notice by the aggrieved person; or (b) a defence has been served in an action brought by the aggrieved person against the
-- publisher in relation to the matter in question."
-- s 16(4): "A renewed offer is to be treated as a new offer (including for the purposes of section 14)." s 16(5): the 28 days
-- do not stop a renewed offer "not in the same terms" if it is "a genuine attempt ... to address matters of concern raised by
-- the aggrieved person about the withdrawn offer" and is made "within 14 days after the withdrawal ... or any other period
-- agreed". Whether the attempt is genuine is a judgment, asked as an input.
DECLARE `The timing of the offer` HAS
    `I gave the publisher a concerns notice`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `days from my concerns notice to the offer`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the publisher had served a defence in my action before the offer`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16(5)
    `it is a genuine attempt to meet my concerns about the withdrawn offer`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 16(5)(a)
    `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer`                          IS A NUMBER    -- s 16(5)(b)
    `days for renewal agreed with me beyond 14`                              IS A NUMBER    -- s 16(5)(b); 0 if none

@export Could the publisher still make me an offer to make amends when it did (ss 14(1), 16(5))?
GIVEN `the timing` IS A `The timing of the offer` @desc When your concerns notice was given, whether a defence had been served, and whether the offer renews a withdrawn one
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the offer to make amends made in time` IF
        (NOT (`the timing`'s `the publisher had served a defence in my action before the offer`))
    AND (    (NOT (`the timing`'s `I gave the publisher a concerns notice`))
          OR `the timing`'s `days from my concerns notice to the offer` LESS THAN 28
          OR (     `the timing`'s `it renews an offer the publisher withdrew, in different terms`
               AND `the timing`'s `it is a genuine attempt to meet my concerns about the withdrawn offer`
               AND `the timing`'s `days from the withdrawal to the renewed offer` AT MOST (14 PLUS `the timing`'s `days for renewal agreed with me beyond 14`)))

§§ `s 15 -- what an offer to make amends must contain`

-- s 15(1): "An offer to make amends -- (a) must be in writing; (b) must be readily identifiable as an offer to make amends
-- under this Division; (c) if the offer is limited to any particular defamatory imputations -- must state that the offer is
-- so limited and particularise the imputations ...; (d) must include an offer to publish, or join in publishing, a reasonable
-- correction ...; (e) if material containing the matter has been given to someone else by the publisher or with the
-- publisher's knowledge -- must include an offer to take, or join in taking, reasonable steps to tell the other person that
-- the matter is or may be defamatory of the aggrieved person; (f) must include an offer to pay the expenses reasonably
-- incurred by the aggrieved person before the offer was made and the expenses reasonably incurred by the aggrieved person in
-- considering the offer". An apology and compensation (s 15(1)(g)) are optional.
DECLARE `The offer` HAS
    `it is in writing`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it is limited to particular imputations`                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `it states the limit and particularises those imputations`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `it offers to publish a reasonable correction`                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `the publisher gave the material to others`                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
    `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others`                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
    `it offers to pay my reasonable expenses before and in considering it`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)

@export Does the publisher's offer contain everything an offer to make amends must (s 15(1)(a)-(f))?
GIVEN `the offer` IS A `The offer` @desc What the publisher's offer says and offers
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` IF
        `the offer`'s `it is in writing`
    AND `the offer`'s `it is readily identifiable as an offer to make amends under the Act`
    AND (    (NOT (`the offer`'s `it is limited to particular imputations`))
          OR `the offer`'s `it states the limit and particularises those imputations`)
    AND `the offer`'s `it offers to publish a reasonable correction`
    AND (    (NOT (`the offer`'s `the publisher gave the material to others`))
          OR `the offer`'s `it offers reasonable steps to tell those others`)
    AND `the offer`'s `it offers to pay my reasonable expenses before and in considering it`

§§ `ss 17, 18 -- accepting or refusing the offer`

-- s 17(1): "If the publisher carries out the terms of an offer to make amends (including payment of any compensation under
-- the offer) that is accepted, the aggrieved person cannot assert, continue or enforce an action for defamation against the
-- publisher in relation to the matter in question even if the offer was limited to any particular defamatory imputations."
-- Until the terms are carried out, the bar has not arisen; a court may decide what must be done to carry them out (s 15(3)).
DECLARE `If I accept` IS ONE OF
    `I can no longer sue this publisher over the matter: the accepted offer has been carried out (s 17(1))`
    `not yet barred: the publisher has not carried out the accepted offer; a court may decide what must be done (s 15(3))`
    `no effect under the Act: it is not an offer to make amends (ss 14, 15)`

@export If I accept the offer to make amends, can I still sue the publisher (s 17(1))?
GIVEN `the timing` IS A `The timing of the offer` @desc When your concerns notice was given, whether a defence had been served, and whether the offer renews a withdrawn one
      `the offer` IS A `The offer` @desc What the publisher's offer says and offers
      `the publisher has carried out its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the publisher has done everything the accepted offer promised, including paying any compensation
GIVETH A `If I accept`
DECIDE `What happens if I accept the offer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`Was the offer to make amends made in time` `the timing`)) OR (NOT (`Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` `the offer`))
            THEN `no effect under the Act: it is not an offer to make amends (ss 14, 15)`
        IF `the publisher has carried out its terms`
            THEN `I can no longer sue this publisher over the matter: the accepted offer has been carried out (s 17(1))`
        OTHERWISE `not yet barred: the publisher has not carried out the accepted offer; a court may decide what must be done (s 15(3))`

-- s 18(1): "If an offer to make amends is made ... but is not accepted, it is a defence ... if -- (a) the publisher made the
-- offer as soon as practicable after becoming aware that the matter is or may be defamatory; (b) at any time before the trial
-- the publisher was ready and willing, on acceptance of the offer by the aggrieved person, to carry out the terms of the
-- offer; and (c) in all the circumstances the offer was reasonable." Each limb is the court's finding, asked as an input.
@export If I refuse the offer to make amends, does the publisher get a defence (s 18(1))?
GIVEN `the timing` IS A `The timing of the offer` @desc When your concerns notice was given, whether a defence had been served, and whether the offer renews a withdrawn one
      `the offer` IS A `The offer` @desc What the publisher's offer says and offers
      `the court finds it was made as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the publisher offered as soon as practicable after learning the matter is or may be defamatory
      `the court finds the publisher was ready and willing to carry it out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the publisher stood ready, before trial, to carry out the offer
      `the court finds the offer was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court finds the offer reasonable in all the circumstances (s 18(2) lists what it weighs)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my refusal give the publisher a defence` IF
        `Was the offer to make amends made in time` `the timing`
    AND `Does the offer meet the requirements of s 15` `the offer`
    AND `the court finds it was made as soon as practicable`
    AND `the court finds the publisher was ready and willing to carry it out`
    AND `the court finds the offer was reasonable`

§§ `ss 25, 26, 31, 33 -- the publisher's defences of truth, opinion and triviality`

-- s 4: "substantially true means true in substance or not materially different from the truth".
-- s 25: "It is a defence ... if the defendant proves that the defamatory imputations carried by the matter of which the
-- plaintiff complains are substantially true."
-- s 26: a defence if the matter carried "other imputations (contextual imputations) that are substantially true" and "the
-- defamatory imputations do not further harm the reputation of the plaintiff because of the substantial truth of the
-- contextual imputations".
-- s 31(1): a defence if "(a) the matter was an expression of opinion of the defendant rather than a statement of fact; (b)
-- the opinion related to a matter of public interest; and (c) the opinion is based on proper material"; s 31(4)(a): it "is
-- defeated if, and only if, the plaintiff proves that ... the opinion was not honestly held by the defendant at the time".
-- s 31(5): "proper material" is material that is substantially true, or was published on a privileged occasion, or under a
-- defence in s 28, 29 or 31 (asked as one finding).
-- s 33: a defence if "the circumstances of publication were such that the plaintiff was unlikely to sustain any harm".
-- Every limb is for the publisher to prove (or for me, in s 31(4)) and for the court to find, so each is an input.
DECLARE `The court's findings on the defences` HAS
    `the imputations I complain of are substantially true`                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 25
    `other imputations in the matter are substantially true`                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 26(a)
    `my imputations do no further harm because of those`                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 26(b)
    `it was the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 31(1)(a)
    `the opinion related to a matter of public interest`                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 31(1)(b)
    `the opinion is based on proper material`                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 31(1)(c), (5)
    `I prove the publisher did not honestly hold the opinion`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 31(4)(a)
    `I was unlikely to sustain any harm in the circumstances of publication`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 33

DECLARE `The defence that defeats me` IS ONE OF
    `justification: the imputations are substantially true (s 25)`
    `contextual truth (s 26)`
    `honest opinion (s 31(1))`
    `triviality (s 33)`
    `none of these defences`

@export Which of the defences of truth, honest opinion or triviality defeats my claim (ss 25, 26, 31, 33)?
GIVEN `the findings` IS A `The court's findings on the defences` @desc What the court finds about the truth of the imputations, whether it was opinion, and the likelihood of harm
GIVETH A `The defence that defeats me`
DECIDE `Which defence defeats my claim` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the findings`'s `the imputations I complain of are substantially true`
            THEN `justification: the imputations are substantially true (s 25)`
        IF     `the findings`'s `other imputations in the matter are substantially true`
           AND `the findings`'s `my imputations do no further harm because of those`
            THEN `contextual truth (s 26)`
        IF     `the findings`'s `it was the publisher's opinion rather than a statement of fact`
           AND `the findings`'s `the opinion related to a matter of public interest`
           AND `the findings`'s `the opinion is based on proper material`
           AND (NOT (`the findings`'s `I prove the publisher did not honestly hold the opinion`))
            THEN `honest opinion (s 31(1))`
        IF `the findings`'s `I was unlikely to sustain any harm in the circumstances of publication`
            THEN `triviality (s 33)`
        OTHERWISE `none of these defences`

§§ `ss 35, 37 -- what I can be awarded`

-- s 35(1): "the maximum amount of damages for noneconomic loss that may be awarded in defamation proceedings is $250 000 or
-- any other amount adjusted in accordance with this section from time to time (the maximum damages amount) that is
-- applicable at the time damages are awarded."
-- s 35(2): the court may award more "if, and only if, the court is satisfied that the circumstances of the publication ...
-- are such as to warrant an award of aggravated damages."
-- s 37: "A plaintiff cannot be awarded exemplary or punitive damages for defamation."
`the maximum damages amount in the Act` MEANS 250000

-- s 35(4): each declared amount is the amount last applicable "adjusted by the percentage change in the amount estimated by
-- the Australian Statistician of the average weekly total earnings of fulltime adults in Australia over the 4 quarters
-- preceding the date of the declaration"; s 35(7): "rounded to the nearest $500" (a half is rounded up: the encoder's
-- reading of "nearest").
@export What will the next maximum damages amount for non-economic loss be (s 35(4), (7))?
GIVEN `the amount last applicable` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount currently applicable ($250,000 if none has been declared)
      `the percentage change in average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The Statistician's percentage change in average weekly total earnings of full-time adults over the 4 quarters, e.g. 3.5 for 3.5%
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What will the next maximum damages amount be` MEANS
    500 TIMES (TRUNC (((`the amount last applicable` TIMES (1 PLUS (`the percentage change in average weekly earnings` DIVIDED BY 100))) PLUS 250) DIVIDED BY 500) 0)

DECLARE `The court's assessment` HAS
    `damages assessed for my economic loss`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `damages assessed for my non-economic loss`                              IS A NUMBER
    `exemplary or punitive damages sought`                                   IS A NUMBER    -- s 37: none can be awarded
    `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 35(2)

@export What is the most I can be awarded for non-economic loss (s 35)?
GIVEN `the assessment` IS A `The court's assessment` @desc The court's assessment of your damages, and whether it finds aggravated damages warranted
      `the maximum damages amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount applicable when damages are awarded (the Minister's latest Gazette order; $250,000 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I get for non-economic loss` MEANS
    IF `the assessment`'s `the court is satisfied aggravated damages are warranted`
        THEN `the assessment`'s `damages assessed for my non-economic loss`
        ELSE `the lesser of` (`the assessment`'s `damages assessed for my non-economic loss`) `the maximum damages amount`

@export How much in damages can I be awarded in all (ss 35, 37)?
GIVEN `the assessment` IS A `The court's assessment` @desc The court's assessment of your damages, and whether it finds aggravated damages warranted
      `the maximum damages amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum damages amount applicable when damages are awarded (the Minister's latest Gazette order; $250,000 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much can I be awarded in all` MEANS
    `the assessment`'s `damages assessed for my economic loss` PLUS `How much can I get for non-economic loss` `the assessment` `the maximum damages amount`
